# Bootowser control sidecar root hooks.
#
# The sidecar runs as the unprivileged kiosk user and escalates only through
# `sudo -n` to the scripts in this directory. The wildcard matches every
# entry directly inside the directory (a forward slash is never matched by
# a sudoers wildcard) and the trailing ` *` passes arbitrary arguments.
#
# Arguments are attacker-controlled whenever the kiosk page is: every script
# in this directory must validate its own arguments like the untrusted input
# they are. Keep scripts root-owned and never group- or world-writable --
# the sidecar re-checks that before every run and refuses otherwise.
bootowser ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/lib/bootowser/commands/* *
